        <h3>About Jungle Walks</h3>
        <p>
            Jungle walks offer an intimate, immersive way to experience Chitwan’s diverse ecosystems. Accompanied by skilled naturalist guides, visitors traverse forest paths, wetlands, and grasslands, spotting wildlife and birds while learning about the flora and fauna.
        </p>

        <h3>What to Expect</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Guided walks lasting about 3 hours, usually in early morning or late afternoon</li>
            <li>Opportunities to see deer, birds, reptiles, and sometimes rhinos or elephants at a safe distance</li>
            <li>Insightful commentary on the local ecosystem, animal behavior, and conservation efforts</li>
            <li>Peaceful time immersed in nature’s sights and sounds</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Trail Routes & Terrain</h3>
        <p>
            The walking routes change seasonally and focus on areas with rich biodiversity. Trails pass through shaded forests, riverbanks, and open grasslands, offering varied terrain and chances to observe different species.
        </p>

        <h3>Highlights</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Close encounters with native wildlife in their natural habitat</li>
            <li>Birdwatching with sightings of both resident and migratory species</li>
            <li>Learning about medicinal plants and local ecology from expert guides</li>
            <li>Enjoying the serene, undisturbed natural environment on foot</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Important Guidelines</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Wear comfortable walking shoes and light, breathable clothing</li>
            <li>Maintain silence and minimize noise to avoid disturbing wildlife</li>
            <li>Follow your guide’s instructions carefully for safety</li>
            <li>Carry water, insect repellent, and a camera for capturing moments</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Interesting Facts</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Jungle walks allow low-impact interaction with nature compared to vehicle safaris</li>
            <li>The trails provide habitat to over 500 bird species and many mammals</li>
            <li>Walking quietly often reveals elusive animals hidden from view during louder activities</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</section>

